# Design system & UI conventions

All theming flows from **`Core/Theme/DesignSystem.swift`** (the `DS` namespace).
A buyer rebrands the whole app by editing values there. **Never hardcode visual
values** — always use a token.

## Tokens (use these, not literals)

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Brand color | `DS.primary`, `DS.accent` |
| Status | `DS.success`, `DS.warning`, `DS.danger`, `DS.info` |
| Text | `DS.Colors.textPrimary` / `.textSecondary` / `.textTertiary` |
| Surfaces | `DS.Colors.background` / `.surface` / `.surfaceSecondary` |
| Lines | `DS.Colors.border`, `DS.Colors.divider` |
| Spacing | `DS.Spacing.xs sm md lg xl xxl xxxl` |
| Radius | `DS.Radius.none xs sm md lg xl xxl full` |
| Shadow | `DS.Shadow.sm/.md/.lg/.xl` |
| Motion | `DS.Motion.fast/.normal/.slow`, `DS.Motion.spring` |
| Border | `DS.Border.thin/.regular/.thick` |

`DS.Colors.*` are adaptive (auto light/dark). Brand colors resolve from
`DS.primaryHex` / `DS.accentHex`.

## Typography

Never call `.font(.system(...))` for app text. Use `.appFont(_:)` with an
`AppTextStyle` case:

```swift
Text("home.title").appFont(.headline)
```

Cases: `largeTitle, title, title2, title3, headline, body, bodyBold, callout,
subheadline, footnote, footnoteSemibold, caption, captionBold, caption2`.
Custom fonts: `Core/Theme/FontRegistry.swift` (set `FontFamily.postScriptName`);
empty = system font.

## Surfaces, cards, buttons

```swift
VStack { … }.dsCard(radius: DS.Radius.lg)      // card with the global SurfaceStyle
VStack { … }.dsCardContent()                    // padded card in one call
TextField("", text: $x).dsInput()               // styled input
Button("Continue") { }.buttonStyle(DSPrimaryButtonStyle())   // Secondary/Ghost/Destructive too
DSEmptyState(title:systemImage:description:)     // reusable empty state
```

`SurfaceStyle` (`.flat .bordered .elevated .glass .liquidGlass`) is global via
`DS.surfaceStyle`, injected as `DSTheme` (`.dsTheme(...)`). `.liquidGlass`
(iOS 26+) falls back to `.glass`.

## PRO — the 10 paywall templates

`Modules/PaywallTemplates/` holds `Template01AnchorDecoy` … `Template10UIShowcase`,
a `PaywallGalleryView` preview browser, `PaywallTemplateHost`, and shared
building blocks in `PaywallComponents.swift`.

They use the **same `DS` tokens** as everything else — they are not a parallel
styling system, and a `DS` retheme restyles all ten. When editing one, prefer
extending `PaywallComponents` over duplicating a subview into a single template.

## PRO — widget views

Files under `Widgets/` belong to the extension target and cannot import
app-only code. `Widgets/Shared` compiles into **both** targets — keep it to
plain shared types (e.g. `ActivityAttributes`). Widget bodies should still use
`DS` tokens where practical so widgets match the app.

## Localization (required for all user-facing text)

Keys live in `Resources/Base.lproj/Localizable.strings` with dotted namespaces:
`home.* settings.* auth.* onb.* notif.* paywall.* ai.* account.* tester.*` and
**PRO** `applock.* charts.* feedback.* language.*`.

```swift
Text("settings.title")                       // LocalizedStringKey
Label("home.tab", systemImage: "house.fill")
String(localized: "home.welcome")
String(localized: "home.welcome.named \(name)")
```

> **PRO — this repo ships four `.lproj` folders: `Base`, `en`, `es`, `hi`.**
> Add every new key to **all four** in the same change. A key present only in
> `Base` renders as the raw key string for a user who switched to Spanish or
> Hindi. Runtime switching is `LocalizationManager.shared` plus
> `.environment(\.locale,…)` and `.id(languageCode)` at the app root.

## Adding a feature screen

1. `Modules/MyFeature/MyFeatureView.swift` (+ ViewModel if it has logic) using
   `DS` + `.appFont` + localization.
2. Add `case myFeature` to `AppRoute`; add a destination in `RootView`.
3. Surface it from `HomeView` via a `HomeSection(title:items:)` item — gate
   behind a feature flag if optional.
4. `xcodegen generate`.

**For a PRO feature, follow `pro-features.mdc` instead** — those are surfaced
from `TestDriveView`/`SettingsView`, not `AppRoute`, so they stay deletable.

Keep `PreviewProvider`s working — views must render with the default container
and local fallbacks (no live keys required).
